From: Gesher Authors
Subject: [PATCH] Report the absence of kernel fs-verity on Windows

The device's initial Android SDK level cannot imply Linux filesystem integrity
support on Windows. The native operations report unsupported; keep the Java
capability query consistent instead of claiming protection is available.

diff --git a/core/java/com/android/internal/security/VerityUtils.java b/core/java/com/android/internal/security/VerityUtils.java
--- a/core/java/com/android/internal/security/VerityUtils.java
+++ b/core/java/com/android/internal/security/VerityUtils.java
@@ -59,3 +59,4 @@
     public static boolean isFsVeritySupported() {
-        return Build.VERSION.DEVICE_INITIAL_SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.R;
+        // Gesher: Windows does not provide Linux kernel-enforced fs-verity.
+        return false;
     }
